  Source: https://github.com/mamedev/mame, tag mame0289 (commit
  f34f02505e32c1993c6a782b6814232cbfc74e36), with frunk.store's changes for
  the browser in engine/mame-web.patch (also tools/mame/mame-web.patch in
  https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose tools/build-mame.mjs
  builds it with Emscripten 6.0.11). The source files the build compiled,
  with MAME's build scripts and the patch applied, are
  engine/mame-0.289-web-src.tar.xz.
  Only the drivers of the games below are built in: exidy/circus,
  exidy/carpolo, exidy/exidy, exidy/starfire, exidy/victory, exidy/vertigo,
  bally/astrocde, bally/gridlee, videogames/supertnk, videogames/looping
  and williams/williams.
  The changes: each animation frame runs the machine for the real time that
  has passed (at most a tenth of a second) rather than a fixed 1/60 s; the
  NVRAM and settings are saved when the machine exits on the web, where
  MAME's own exit path never runs, and web_save() saves them at once for a
  page that's being left; and the build exports the file system and links
  IndexedDB storage for them.

Games
  None are included. Their ROM images are released by their owners for
  free, non-commercial use through mamedev.org
  (https://www.mamedev.org/roms/), which alone may distribute them. Each
  player downloads them there and sends them to their own car; frunk.store
  never stores or passes them on, and the phone transfer that carries them
  is encrypted end to end and deleted on arrival.

